# justccell.com — production-only workflow (dev paused)

## Default target

All implementation, fixes, and QA for `websites/justccell.com` ship to **justccell.com (production)** only.

- **Hostinger path:** `public_html/wp-content/themes/justccell-theme/`
- **TUS relative prefix:** `wp-content/themes/justccell-theme/{file}`
- **Account:** `u392808260` · WP software id **`30055979`**

## dev.justccell.com — paused

**Do not deploy to, test on, or reference dev as the completion target** until the user explicitly re-enables dev after production go-live.

Managing two WordPress installs during pre-launch optimization was paused by owner decision (2026-09-06). The dev clone may be stale; treat **production + vault** as the single source of truth.

When dev is re-enabled later, update this rule and `docs/dev-environment.md` in the same turn.

## Production deploy

After coding, patch production via in-place TUS (see `.cursor/rules/justccell-auto-deploy.mdc`). Do not ask “want me to deploy?” — production deploy is included.

## Pre-launch visibility (production)

Keep **discourage search engines** and **coming soon / maintenance** active on production until go-live is approved. Spec: `websites/justccell.com/docs/dev-environment.md` (visibility section).

## CSS / UI work

Before writing or editing storefront CSS for Justccell, read and follow the **UI UX Pro Max** skill (`~/.cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/SKILL.md`). Reference: https://ui-ux-pro-max-skill.nextlevelbuilder.io/

**wp-admin:** never enqueue storefront CSS in admin; never override core modals/dialogs with theme CSS (`rules.md` §13).

